<b>EARTH TAG - PRIVACY POLICY</b>
Last updated: 11/25/26

This Privacy Policy explains what information Earth Tag (the "game") collects, how it is used and shared, and the choices you have. "We" and "us" means thatonelem, United States. Contact: thatonelem@gmail.com.

<b>1. What we collect</b>

<b>From your Meta account</b>
- your Meta user ID and Meta username, to sign you in
- a one-time sign-in check from Meta that confirms your account is real
- whether you own the Game
- which in-game items you have bought. We never see your payment details.

<b>From Epic Online Services (EOS)</b>
- an EOS player ID linked to your Meta account
- your username
- your items and cosmetics
- whether your account is active

<b>When you play online</b>
- your username, color, cosmetics and movement are sent to the other players in your server so they can see you
- servers you create: the server name, whether it is private, its code, and the place it is set to
- voice chat: your microphone audio is sent live to the other players in your server.
- your IP address and connection details, obscured by Epic's network services to connect you to other players

<b>When you pick a place on Earth</b>
- text you type into the place search, and the places you visit. Searches go to our location service, hosted on AWS.
- to show 3D maps, your headset downloads map data from Cesium and Google. They receive your IP address and which areas you are viewing.
- the Game does NOT use your headset's real location.

<b>Saved only on your headset</b>
- your settings, username, color, and when you accepted these terms
- videos you record with the in-game camera, if you have it

<b>Microphone</b>
The Game asks for microphone permission for voice chat. You can turn it off at any time in your Quest settings. The game still works, but other players will not hear you.

<b>2. How we use it</b>
- to sign you in and run online play, servers and voice chat
- to give you the items you bought
- to keep players safe: enforcing our Terms of Service, looking into reports and banning accounts
- to fix bugs and keep the game running
We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for targeted advertising.

<b>3. Who we share it with</b>
- other players: your username, avatar, voice, and anything you say or do in a server
- companies:
  - Meta Platforms (sign-in, store, purchases): meta.com/privacy
  - Epic Games (Epic Online Services: accounts, servers, networking, storage, bans): epicgames.com/privacypolicy
  - Amazon Web Services (place search, backend)
  - Cesium and Google (3D maps)
  - Unity Technologies (game engine; may collect crash information)
- anyone the law requires us to share it with, or when needed to protect someone's safety

<b>4. Why we are allowed to use it (UK and EU players)</b>
- to provide the Game you asked to play (contract)
- to keep the Game safe and working (legitimate interests)
- your microphone, only with your permission (consent)

<b>5. How long we keep it</b>
- EOS account and saved data: until you contact us
- data on your headset: until you uninstall the Game

<b>6. Children</b>
The Game is for players aged 13 and over. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you think a child under 13 has given us personal information, contact us and we will delete it.

<b>7. Your choices and rights</b>
- change your username in the Game at any time
- turn off your microphone in your Quest settings
- ask us for a copy of your data, or ask us to correct or delete it: email thatonelem@gmail.com with your username and Meta username
- depending on where you live (for example the UK, EU or California), you may have more rights, including the right to complain to your data protection authority (in the UK: the Information Commissioner's Office, ico.org.uk)

<b>8. Security</b>
We rely on the security of the companies listed above to protect your data, but no online service is completely secure.

<b>9. Data outside your country</b>
The companies we use may handle data in other countries, including the United States.

<b>10. Changes</b>
If we change this Privacy Policy in an important way, the Game will ask you to accept the new version before you play again.

